Description: power-user utilities for Linux Mint Cinnamon
 TuxToys is a set of small desktop tools for Linux Mint Cinnamon, inspired
 by Microsoft PowerToys, each switched on or off in one place and built on
 what Cinnamon already provides.
 .
 This release carries sixteen tools: Awake keeps the computer from sleeping
 without changing the power settings; Light Switch switches between Linux
 Mint's day and dark modes on a schedule; Hosts File Editor edits /etc/hosts;
 Environment Variables sets your variables, profiles of them, and the
 system's; Always on Top keeps a window above the others, framed; Color
 Picker picks a color from the screen; Screen Ruler measures what is on it;
 Text Extractor copies the text in any part of it; Shortcut Guide shows
 Cinnamon's keyboard shortcuts and the active app's; Find My Mouse shows
 where the pointer is, Mouse Highlighter your clicks and Mouse Pointer
 Crosshairs lines through it; File Locksmith shows which processes hold a
 file open; New+ manages the templates of Nemo's Create New Document; Image
 Resizer resizes pictures and Rename+ renames many files at once, both from
 Nemo's right-click menu. They come with a panel icon, a settings window and
 the tuxtoys command.
